From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: prospero-win <prospero-win@invalid>
Date: Fri, 9 Oct 2026 21:40:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] winebus: Show the PS5 title's controller as a HID gamepad.

XInput games reach the DualSense through xinput's own bridge to the
title (patch 0470), but DirectInput, winmm, Raw Input and
Windows.Gaming.Input only find controllers among the HID devices
winebus makes, and a title had none: Undertale's joystick setup and
modern Unity games (Sektori) saw no controller.

winebus gains a PS5 bus (bus_ps5.c). Its init finds the title's pad
calls (pw_wine_pad, pw_wine_set_rumble) with dlsym, as xinput does,
and fails anywhere else. It makes one device, always present: an
Xbox 360 controller (045e:028e, "Controller (XBOX 360 For Windows)")
with hid_device_add_gamepad's layout, so the HID stack gives it the
&IG_ gamepad interface and winexinput its &XI_ partner. The bus thread
reads the pad every 4 ms and sends a report when it changed; a
disconnected pad reads neutral. Rumble reaches the title through the
haptics report, and stops at the report's cutoff (1 s by default)
unless renewed, as with SDL's timed rumble. With the PS5 bus running, winebus makes no virtual
mouse or keyboard and starts no other bus: a title's keyboard and
mouse reach Wine through the user driver.

XInput still reads the title directly and does not use this device,
so XInput games see one controller.
